Real-Time Chat App

A simple real-time chat application that allows users to join chat rooms and exchange messages instantly using WebSockets.

📸 Overview

The application provides a room-based chat experience:

Users enter a Room ID to join a chat room.
Multiple users can join the same room.
Messages are delivered to all users in the same room in real time.
WebSockets maintain a persistent connection between the client and server.
Messages are displayed differently depending on whether they were sent by the current user or another participant.
✨ Features
🔗 Room-based chat — Join a specific room using a Room ID.
⚡ Real-time messaging — Messages are delivered instantly using WebSockets.
👥 Multiple users — Multiple clients can communicate within the same room.
💬 Live message updates — No page refresh is required to receive messages.
🎨 Responsive chat interface — Simple and clean chat-room UI.
🔄 Persistent WebSocket connection — Enables continuous two-way communication between client and server.
🏗️ How It Works

The application follows a simple client-server architecture:

┌──────────────┐
│    Client    │
│              │
│  Join Room   │
│  Send Message│
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       │ WebSocket
       ▼
┌────────────────────┐
│   WebSocket Server │
│                    │
│  Room Management   │
│  Message Routing   │
└─────────┬──────────┘
          │
          │ Broadcast
          ▼
   ┌───────────────┐
   │ Users in Room │
   └───────────────┘

Room Logic

When a client connects, it can join a room by providing a Room ID.

The server maintains a collection of rooms and their connected clients.

For example:

Room A
 ├── Client 1
 ├── Client 2
 └── Client 3

Room B
 ├── Client 4
 └── Client 5


When Client 1 sends a message in Room A, the server broadcasts that message only to the clients connected to Room A.

Clients in Room B do not receive the message.

🔄 Message Flow
The user enters a Room ID.
The client establishes a WebSocket connection with the server.
The client sends a request to join the specified room.
The server adds the client to that room.
When the user sends a message, it is sent through the WebSocket.
The server receives the message.
The server broadcasts the message to other clients in the same room.
Connected clients receive the message and update their chat interface immediately.
User
  │
  │ Send message
  ▼
Client
  │
  │ WebSocket
  ▼
Server
  │
  │ Find user's room
  ▼
Room
  │
  │ Broadcast message
  ▼
Other connected clients

